{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145970",
      "title": "Creating & Using Dynamic API Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 324,
      "videoOrder": 301,
      "sourceHash": "8d5da56d169d78c36084456d125333cc593dcba7a4bef8cdb11a39e8f013ec1e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.08,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "Okay, so now we also know how",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 7.073,
          "en": "to work with our API routes inside of getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.91,
          "end": 9.59,
          "en": "We don't send the request there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.59,
          "end": 13.9,
          "en": "we just execute the code directly in getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.9,
          "end": 16.58,
          "en": "or getServiceAddProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.58,
          "end": 20.4,
          "en": "Now let's talk about dynamic API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.4,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "What's that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 26.06,
          "en": "Well, let's say you don't just wanna have /api/feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.06,
          "end": 28.39,
          "en": "which handles post and get requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.39,
          "end": 33.39,
          "en": "but you also wanna support /api/feedback/some feedback ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.51,
          "end": 37.64,
          "en": "to just fetched a single piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.64,
          "end": 41.76,
          "en": "of data for that specific feedback item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.76,
          "end": 44.56,
          "en": "because maybe you need that somewhere on your page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.56,
          "end": 48.04,
          "en": "For example, on the feedback page, you could say that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.04,
          "end": 50.59,
          "en": "for every list item you're rendering here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.59,
          "end": 55.31,
          "en": "you also have like a show details button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.31,
          "end": 56.91,
          "en": "And when that button is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.91,
          "end": 60.56,
          "en": "you wanna show the details for that feedback item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.56,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "And hence you want to fetch the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 65.63,
          "en": "the full data for that feedback item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.63,
          "end": 66.463,
          "en": "Now we are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.463,
          "end": 69.12,
          "en": "of course actually fetching the full feedback data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.12,
          "end": 72.98,
          "en": "And we could just use client inside JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.98,
          "end": 76.49,
          "en": "to use that already loaded data for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.49,
          "end": 80.15,
          "en": "But let's assume that we're not fetching the full data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.15,
          "end": 82.63,
          "en": "but that instead we are only getting the ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.63,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "and the text and not the email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "And therefore when this button is clicked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 89.99,
          "en": "we wanna fetch the full data again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.99,
          "end": 92.87,
          "en": "but not for all feedback items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.87,
          "end": 95.77000000000001,
          "en": "but for this single feedback item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.77000000000001,
          "end": 99.52000000000001,
          "en": "And that's what you could use a dynamic API route for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.52000000000001,
          "end": 102.72999999999999,
          "en": "because we already know dynamic pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.72999999999999,
          "end": 104.77000000000001,
          "en": "where you create a page with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.77000000000001,
          "end": 109.58,
          "en": "that square bracket notation, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.58,
          "end": 111,
          "en": "This would then allow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111,
          "end": 116,
          "en": "for a request sent to /feedback/some-id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116,
          "end": 118.9,
          "en": "And some-id would be interpreted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.9,
          "end": 122.42,
          "en": "as a value for this ID placeholder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.42,
          "end": 126.63,
          "en": "and you could then use it inside of that page component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.63,
          "end": 127.64,
          "en": "and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.64,
          "end": 130,
          "en": "That's what we already learned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130,
          "end": 132.71,
          "en": "Now that's for regular pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.71,
          "end": 136.76,
          "en": "We can use a similar feature for API routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.76,
          "end": 139.43,
          "en": "because it's also not unrealistic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.43,
          "end": 143.11,
          "en": "that we wanna send the request to /api/feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.11,
          "end": 146.86,
          "en": "and then the ID of a specific feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.86,
          "end": 150.56,
          "en": "to then load the data for that specific feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.56,
          "end": 153.25,
          "en": "And for this, we need a new file because here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.25,
          "end": 156.26,
          "en": "in feedback.js, we only handle the requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.26,
          "end": 160.39,
          "en": "to /api/feedback/nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.39,
          "end": 162.32,
          "en": "Hence in the API folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.32,
          "end": 166.27,
          "en": "we can add a dynamic API route and we do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.27,
          "end": 170.61,
          "en": "in exactly the same way as we do it for a regular pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.61,
          "end": 174.25,
          "en": "We use square brackets and then any place holder name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.25,
          "end": 179.01,
          "en": "of our choice, like for example id or feedbackId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.01,
          "end": 180.77,
          "en": "or whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.77,
          "end": 183.4,
          "en": "And I'll go with feedbackId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.4,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "So now we have a dynamic API route file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "In there, we still define our handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 192.55,
          "en": "and we still export that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.55,
          "end": 194.57,
          "en": "So just as in the other file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.57,
          "end": 197.25,
          "en": "because it works in exactly the same way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.25,
          "end": 200.37,
          "en": "This API route works in exactly the same way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.37,
          "end": 201.73,
          "en": "it's just dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.73,
          "end": 204.76,
          "en": "So for dynamic path segments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.76,
          "end": 208.21,
          "en": "So therefore in here, we might now want to fetch the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.21,
          "end": 210.88,
          "en": "for a specific piece of feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.88,
          "end": 211.76,
          "en": "And for that of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.76,
          "end": 216.59,
          "en": "we need to know which concrete value was encoded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.59,
          "end": 221.43,
          "en": "in the URL as a value for this placeholder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.43,
          "end": 222.69,
          "en": "And we can get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.69,
          "end": 226.55,
          "en": "to that again, through this request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.55,
          "end": 230.15,
          "en": "which we should accept together with that response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.15,
          "end": 232.6,
          "en": "And there, we learned that we have body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.6,
          "end": 235.49,
          "en": "for accessing the submitted data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.49,
          "end": 238.71,
          "en": "method for finding out which kind of request it was.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.71,
          "end": 241.82,
          "en": "And we also have query for getting access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.82,
          "end": 245.49,
          "en": "to query parameters and regular parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.49,
          "end": 249.177,
          "en": "So we can get access and get our feedbackId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.76,
          "end": 253.023,
          "en": "by accessing req.query.feedbackId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.468,
          "end": 258.43,
          "en": ".feedbackId because I encoded feedbackId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.43,
          "end": 261.963,
          "en": "between the square brackets here in my file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.89,
          "end": 265.89,
          "en": "So that gives us access to the concrete feedbackId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.89,
          "end": 268.56,
          "en": "that was part of the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.56,
          "end": 271.41,
          "en": "when that request hit that handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.41,
          "end": 273.65999999999997,
          "en": "And now we can use that feedbackId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.65999999999997,
          "end": 276.58,
          "en": "to retrieve a specific feedback item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.58,
          "end": 278.563,
          "en": "from the feedback json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.69,
          "end": 283.13,
          "en": "For this, I still wanna get access to that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 283.13,
          "end": 286.87,
          "en": "So I will still import my two functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 286.87,
          "end": 288.89,
          "en": "from that other file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288.89,
          "end": 293.622,
          "en": "So from the feedback.js file, the buildFeedbackPath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 293.622,
          "end": 296.81,
          "en": "and the extractFeedback functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 296.81,
          "end": 298.52,
          "en": "again we could outsource them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 298.52,
          "end": 302.36,
          "en": "in some global helpers file if we wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 302.36,
          "end": 304.26,
          "en": "And then I'll construct my file path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 304.26,
          "end": 306.71,
          "en": "by calling buildFeedbackPath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.71,
          "end": 311.71,
          "en": "and get my feedbackData by calling extractFeedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.99,
          "end": 317.39,
          "en": "and passing file path as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.39,
          "end": 320.9,
          "en": "Now, feedbackData is then an array of all items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.9,
          "end": 321.733,
          "en": "And now here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.733,
          "end": 325.16,
          "en": "I just want to get all the data for one specific item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 325.16,
          "end": 327.07,
          "en": "So since this is an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 327.07,
          "end": 330.76,
          "en": "we can of course just call feedbackData.find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330.76,
          "end": 332.62,
          "en": "to find one single item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.81,
          "end": 336.59000000000003,
          "en": "which then executes a function on every item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336.59000000000003,
          "end": 337.423,
          "en": "to find out whether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.423,
          "end": 340.03,
          "en": "that is the item we're looking for or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 340.03,
          "end": 344.46,
          "en": "And the item we're looking for is the item where feedback.id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 344.46,
          "end": 347.413,
          "en": "is equal to feedbackId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 349.02,
          "end": 351.013,
          "en": "So that is then the selectedFeedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 352.67,
          "end": 354.97,
          "en": "And that's the kind of data we now want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 354.97,
          "end": 358.933,
          "en": "to send back with that for incoming requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 359.86,
          "end": 362.12,
          "en": "And for this, we used the response object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 362.12,
          "end": 366.97,
          "en": "set a status of 200 and set our json response body data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 368.27,
          "end": 370.97,
          "en": "which could carry an items key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 370.97,
          "end": 374.34,
          "en": "which is an object here where I set the feedback key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 374.34,
          "end": 377.12,
          "en": "lets say, to selectedFeedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.3,
          "end": 382.15,
          "en": "And now that would return a feedback for a selected ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 382.15,
          "end": 384.59,
          "en": "Now, just to make that crystal clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 384.59,
          "end": 386.56,
          "en": "your dynamic API routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 386.56,
          "end": 389.15,
          "en": "cannot just handle get requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 389.15,
          "end": 392.04,
          "en": "Here, I'm not checking the request method at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 392.04,
          "end": 394.72,
          "en": "which means that for all incoming requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 394.72,
          "end": 397.68,
          "en": "I'm just sending back this json data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 397.68,
          "end": 400.32,
          "en": "But we could all check the request method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 400.32,
          "end": 402.65999999999997,
          "en": "and do something different for post requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 402.65999999999997,
          "end": 404.19,
          "en": "if we needed to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 404.19,
          "end": 406.76,
          "en": "For example, you could check for delete requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 406.76,
          "end": 411.65999999999997,
          "en": "And if a delete request is sent for a specific feedback ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 411.65999999999997,
          "end": 414.22,
          "en": "you could execute some code that deletes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 414.22,
          "end": 417.71,
          "en": "that feedback from our stored feedback items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 417.71,
          "end": 420.16,
          "en": "It's not a functionality I need here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 420.16,
          "end": 422.4,
